<task id="021" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-07: Description becomes Profile, populated from the record</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>013+015 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx/.ts client code and reads a new field set across the BFF Office surface; tags include frontend + bff-api.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Closed, fully-enumerated requirement: four fields plus seven status states, all verified live. No architectural judgment required.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>013,015</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, bff-api, office-addins, dataverse, ai-profile</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Rename the pane's "Description" section to "Profile" and populate it read-only from the identified `sprk_document` record: `sprk_filesummary`, `sprk_filetldr`, `sprk_filekeywords`, `sprk_documenttype`. When `sprk_filesummarystatus` is anything other than Completed, render that state explicitly instead of four blank fields.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in React 19 + Fluent UI v9 task-pane views, Dataverse choice-column semantics, and the BFF `/api/office` read surface. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>The Save tab carries a "Profile" section that, for a document identity resolved by task 013, displays the four profile fields when profiling completed, and displays an honest state message for each of the other six `sprk_filesummarystatus` values. All fields are read-only in the pane. A contract test covers whatever read surface supplies the fields.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-07 requires: rename "Description" to "Profile"; populate `sprk_filesummary`, `sprk_filetldr`, `sprk_filekeywords`, `sprk_documenttype` from the record; and for a non-complete `sprk_filesummarystatus`, show that state rather than blank fields.

      Verified as-built (do not re-derive):
      - All four profile fields exist on `sprk_document`.
      - `sprk_filesummarystatus` is a CHOICE with exactly SEVEN values: None (100000000), Pending (100000001), Completed (100000002), Opted Out (100000003), Failed (100000004), Not Supported (100000005), Skipped (100000006). The pane must render all seven, not just Completed.
      - The pane's current "Description" section is a free-text `Textarea` at `SaveFlow.tsx:862-875` bound to `documentDescription` state at `:424`. That control is an INPUT for `sprk_documentdescription`, which is a different column from the profile fields. Decide and state in the PR whether the free-text description input is retained alongside the Profile section or removed; do not silently conflate the two.
      - Per spec Assumptions, PROFILE FIELDS ARE READ-ONLY IN THE PANE. Editing happens in the record via FR-10 (task 027). Do not add edit affordances to the four profile fields.
      - The BFF already knows these fields: `DocumentProfileFieldMapper` maps "summary"/"tl;dr"/"keywords" onto them, and `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:808-817` writes them. What does not yet exist is a pane-facing READ of them keyed by document id.
      - Task 013 supplies the resolved document identity; without it there is nothing to read and the section must render its no-identity state.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/SaveView.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/DocumentProfileSection.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useDocumentProfile.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/DocumentProfileFieldMapper.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/todoChoices.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">FR-01 client identity wiring — supplies the resolved `sprk_document` id that this section reads its profile from.</dependency>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">FR-03 tab shell — the Save tab frame this section renders inside.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — within this task the four profile fields are strictly READ-ONLY in the pane (spec Assumptions). MUST NOT add inline editing, a pencil affordance, or a save-back for `sprk_filesummary`, `sprk_filetldr`, `sprk_filekeywords`, or `sprk_documenttype`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the status rendering must cover all SEVEN `sprk_filesummarystatus` values: None (100000000), Pending (100000001), Completed (100000002), Opted Out (100000003), Failed (100000004), Not Supported (100000005), Skipped (100000006). A `default` branch that lumps six states into one generic message does not satisfy FR-07.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — mirror the choice-value table locally in the add-in the way `shared/taskpane/services/todoChoices.ts` does. That file is the sanctioned duplicate precedent for exactly this reason (no Xrm in an Office host). MUST NOT introduce a second, divergent copy of a table this project already owns elsewhere in the add-in.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE — the document GUID this section reads by MUST be canonicalized bare-lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid` before it crosses any boundary, and MUST NOT be interpolated raw into an OData key predicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE — for all Profile-section UI: Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only, no hex literals, and the section (including every status state) honors the Office light/dark theme via `useOfficeTheme`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE — for this add-in package only: per this project's Path A exception, the Profile section is a thin view under `shared/taskpane/`. MUST NOT import `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-03: `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host. MUST NOT import any Xrm-bound component. Recreate the layout, per the r2 precedent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE — if this task adds or modifies a read route on `/api/office`, authorization goes on an endpoint filter on the group, never inside the handler body.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE — any endpoint this task adds or modifies gets a contract test in `tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs`. Cite `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` — there is no concise copy in `.claude/adr/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — BFF publish size: measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF `origin/master`, never against the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Zip both with PowerShell `Compress-Archive` and report both absolute sizes, the delta, and the tool name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the PR description MUST state the Placement Justification for every BFF-side change, per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — run `/conflict-check` before opening any BFF-touching PR. `spaarkeai-compose-r8` and `unified-access-control-r2` are live on this same hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — build commands for `src/client/office-addins` only: install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; there is NO `build:prod` script — `npm run build` IS the production build.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Document profile fields, Dataverse choice columns, Fluent v9 in an Office host</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/plan.md</file>
