      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins. Long summary text must wrap and scroll inside the narrow pane rather than forcing horizontal overflow.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Read before adding any read route to `/api/office`; the group already carries `.RequireAuthorization()`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md, spec.md FR-07, and the knowledge files above. Output the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL) per root CLAUDE.md §8.</step>
    <step order="1">Determine the read surface. Grep the existing `/api/office` and `/api/documents` routes for one that already returns the four profile fields plus `sprk_filesummarystatus` for a document id. Extend an existing route if one is close; only add a route if none is. Record the decision and the grep evidence in the PR (CLAUDE.md §11).</step>
    <step order="2">Build the seven-state status table in the add-in, mirroring the `todoChoices.ts` precedent, with an explicit user-facing message per state. Do not use a catch-all default.</step>
    <step order="3">Build `DocumentProfileSection.tsx` and `useDocumentProfile.ts`: read-only rendering of summary, TL;DR, keywords, and document type, plus the per-status states, plus a no-identity state when task 013 resolved nothing.</step>
    <step order="4">Rename the section heading from "Description" to "Profile" in `SaveFlow.tsx` and decide the fate of the free-text description input; state the decision in the PR.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire the section into the Save tab through `SaveView.tsx`, threading the identity from task 013 rather than re-resolving it.</step>
    <step order="6">Add or update the contract test in `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs` for the read surface, including the unauthorized case.</step>
    <step order="7">Add unit tests covering all seven status renderings plus the no-identity state.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`; run `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests. All green.</step>
    <step order="9">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the constraint above; record both absolute sizes, the delta, and the zip tool.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check`, then code-review + adr-check per task-execute Step 9.5.</step>
    <step order="11">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If no existing route returns the profile fields and a NEW BFF route is required, STOP before writing it and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the §11 three-question answers (existing / extension / cost-of-doing-nothing) and the grep evidence, so the placement decision is made explicitly rather than absorbed.</trigger>
    <trigger>If `sprk_filesummarystatus` returns a value outside the seven enumerated options, STOP and escalate rather than adding a catch-all branch — the option set has changed and this task's closed acceptance set is no longer correct.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: the free-text "Description" Textarea at `src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx:862-875`, bound to `documentDescription` at `:424`. Grep run: `grep -rn "sprk_filesummary\b|sprk_filetldr|sprk_filekeywords|sprk_filesummarystatus" --include=*.cs src/server` returns writers (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:808-817`) and a mapper (`Services/Ai/DocumentProfileFieldMapper.cs`) but NO pane-facing reader keyed by document id.</existing>
    <extension>Partly. The section heading and layout extend the existing Document Details card rather than adding a new surface; the new `DocumentProfileSection` component exists because the existing control is a free-text INPUT bound to a different column (`sprk_documentdescription`) and cannot render seven read-only status states.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this, a user who saved a document to Spaarke sees an empty "Description" box in the pane and has no way to tell whether the AI profile succeeded, is still pending, failed, or was skipped — the exact blank-fields complaint FR-07 names. The Generate Profile button (task 022) also has nothing to reflect its result into.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Completed profile renders all four fields">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Spaarke-sourced Word document whose `sprk_filesummarystatus` is Completed (100000002).</step>
        <step>Observe the Profile section on the Save tab.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Summary, TL;DR, keywords, and document type all display with their record values; the section heading reads "Profile", not "Description"; none of the four is editable.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="All six non-Completed states render honestly">
      <steps>
        <step>For each of None, Pending, Opted Out, Failed, Not Supported, and Skipped, seed a document with that `sprk_filesummarystatus` value and open the pane.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each state shows its own distinct message naming the state; none of the six renders four blank fields, and none falls through to a shared generic message.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="No-identity state">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a document that did not originate from Spaarke, so task 013 resolves no identity, and view the Save tab.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Profile section shows a no-identity state explaining that the document is not yet in Spaarke; it does not show empty profile fields and does not error.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode check via the Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office theme to Dark and reload the pane; view the Profile section in the Completed state and in the Failed state.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All text, dividers, keyword chips, and status indicators resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens with legible contrast in dark mode; no hex literals; repeat in Light mode with the same result.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Long summary does not break the pane layout">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a document whose `sprk_filesummary` is several paragraphs and narrow the pane to its minimum width.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The summary wraps and scrolls vertically inside the section; the pane never scrolls horizontally.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF and run the Office contract tests.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Install with --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; typecheck, test, and build (build IS production here).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/DocumentProfileSection.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useDocumentProfile.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/__tests__/DocumentProfileSection.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/021-publish-size.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a document with `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Completed (100000002), when the Save tab renders, then `sprk_filesummary`, `sprk_filetldr`, `sprk_filekeywords`, and `sprk_documenttype` all display their record values.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = None (100000000), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a state message naming that state and does not show four blank fields.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Pending (100000001), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a distinct in-progress state message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Opted Out (100000003), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a distinct opted-out state message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Failed (100000004), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a distinct failure state message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Not Supported (100000005), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a distinct not-supported state message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `sprk_filesummarystatus` = Skipped (100000006), when the Save tab renders, then the pane shows a distinct skipped state message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given any status value, when the Profile section renders, then none of the four profile fields is editable and no save-back control for them exists in the pane.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the section heading, when the Save tab renders, then it reads "Profile"; the string "Description" no longer labels this section.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a document with no resolved identity, when the Save tab renders, then the Profile section shows an explicit no-identity state and makes no profile read call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unauthenticated or unauthorized caller, when the profile read route is invoked, then it returns 401/403 as a ProblemDetails response, not an unhandled error — asserted by a contract test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office theme set to Dark, when the Profile section renders in any state, then every color resolves from a Fluent v9 semantic token and no hex literal appears in the added styles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean for the files this task touched; `npm test` and `npm run build` pass; `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size is measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`, both absolute sizes and the delta are recorded, and the delta is under the +5 MB escalation threshold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-07 + Assumptions ("Profile fields are read-only in the pane"); plan.md §4 Phase 2 task 021. Profiling itself works — #919 was fixed on master (`f5c7687d8`) — so a Completed status is reachable in a seeded environment. Task 022 adds the Generate Profile trigger that moves a document between these states; keep the status rendering in this task the single place that maps a status value to a message so 022 does not fork it.
  </notes>

